{
  "answer": "**Short answer:** the frontend treats \"logged in\" as \"a token string exists in localStorage.\" It does not check the token's validity or expiry. Expired or invalid tokens are handled reactively, when the backend rejects a request.\n\n**Deciding logged-in state**\n- `isLoggedIn()` returns `localStorage.getItem(\"access_token\") !== null` (`frontend/src/hooks/useAuth.ts:14-16`).\n- `useAuth` fetches the current user via `UsersService.readUserMe` only when `isLoggedIn()` is true (`frontend/src/hooks/useAuth.ts:23-27`).\n- The protected layout route calls `isLoggedIn()` at `frontend/src/routes/_layout.tsx:15`. The call graph confirms this, but I could not read the redirect body there, so I can't say exactly where it sends the user.\n\n**Attaching the token**\n- Each request runs through `beforeRequest` (`frontend/src/client/client/client.gen.ts:38-67`), which calls `setAuthParams` (`frontend/src/client/client/utils.gen.ts:86-125`). That writes the token into the `Authorization` header. I did not confirm where the token value is read from.\n\n**Expired or invalid tokens**\n- `handleApiError` in `frontend/src/main.tsx:22-30` handles 401 and 403 responses. It removes `access_token` from localStorage and sets `window.location.href = \"/login\"`.\n- **Gap:** the call graph shows no callers for `handleApiError`. I could not confirm it is registered on the query/mutation cache, so I can't confirm that path runs. If it isn't wired up, an expired token leaves the user on the page with failed requests.\n- Logout (`frontend/src/hooks/useAuth.ts:56-59`) only removes the token and navigates to `/login`. It does not call the backend.\n- Login stores the token from `/login/access-token` (`frontend/src/hooks/useAuth.ts:41-46`).\n\n**Net effect:** a stale token keeps `isLoggedIn()` true until a request returns 401/403. Whether the user is then redirected depends on the unverified `handleApiError` wiring.",
